// netboot relocation trampoline — reference source.
//
// Assembled ONLY to extract its machine-code words (it is not loaded the normal
// way).  netboot.c embeds these words, relocates the two absolute jump targets
// to the high run address, patches the len/entry immediates, copies the staged
// image down to 0x0, and jumps to the program entry.
//
// Registers: A=src  B=dst  C=len(bytes)  D=entry  E=tmp  F=stack-top
//
// SETSP F restores SP=0x0800_0000 before the jump — exactly what the hardware
// loader's LOAD_COMPLETE does, so the program sees the same initial SP.
// See netboot.c TRAMP_* constants for the word indices that get patched.
_start
SETR A 0x4000000
SETR B 0x0
SETR C 0x0
SETR D 0x0
SETR F 0x8000000
LOOP:
CMPRV C 0
JMPE DONE:
MEMGET64 E A
MEMSET64 E B
ADDV A 8
ADDV B 8
MINUSV C 8
JMP LOOP:
DONE:
SETSP F
JMPR D
